<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">23 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">23 CE in world history: 2 events, 3 deaths and 1 state that came to an end. 151 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/42-bce">42 BCE</a><a href="/years/31-bce">31 BCE</a><a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a><a href="/years/27-bce">27 BCE</a><a href="/years/23" aria-current="page">23 CE</a><a href="/years/69">69 CE</a><a href="/years/224">224 CE</a><a href="/years/260">260 CE</a><a href="/years/328">328 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/changan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-4">4 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lülin rebels sack Chang'an, the capital of Wang Mang's Xin dynasty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lulin">Lülin</a> peasant rebellion, rebels captured and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>'s short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a>; Wang Mang was killed two days later. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> government later made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> its primary capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lulin">Lülin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/changan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-6">6 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rebels kill Wang Mang as Chang'an falls</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel forces broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-mang">Wang Mang</a>, the usurper who had founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xin-dynasty">Xin dynasty</a>. His death cleared the way for the restoration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-guangwu-of-han">Emperor Guangwu</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
